{"title":"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(n_as_largest)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (n as largest)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(n_as_middle)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (n as middle)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Verifying_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Verifying Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of three consecutive integers is 153. The largest of these three integers is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/b/a1bb7c35e850154eefdd95362f3343868b1ecba1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 52 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 50 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 53 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 54 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 51$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28n_as_largest.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(n_as_largest)\">Solution 1 (n as largest)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (n as largest)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the largest number of the three integers. Since the numbers are consecutive, the whole list is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/9/e69cf53645b4d4589764f6594d01814e5f18ca8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - 2, n - 1, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"17\" />. The sum of all three integers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f152e2688863b88e971932e82c28adec9063a05e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$153$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e4054fd912f33996a5cc10a6ef61a5971e6c80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - 2 + n - 1 + n = 153$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"193\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/c/76c9b56028ef93aef222e8859a72b4238a88c84b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n - 3 = 153$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/1/951abc23783ab9130ee1b94feeeecd6ba2e9a115.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n = 153 + 3 = 156$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/6/326c02c48a5fe208a07fc9e285c63ea9107e7bf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\frac{156}{3} = \\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } 52}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"158\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28n_as_middle.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(n_as_middle)\">Solution 2 (n as middle)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (n as middle)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the middle number of the three. Since the numbers are consecutive integers, the whole list is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/1/681796667279a4909e9687bc2dc1f9c295ecf84a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - 1, n, n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"17\" />. The sum of all three integers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f152e2688863b88e971932e82c28adec9063a05e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$153$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/a/11ae698cb44e0b7850bd3ac81f1853150497c924.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - 1 + n + n + 1 = 153$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"193\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/0/e50b319e78fd249f9d484494070d960bb513c0fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n = 153$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/2130e03c516b9c7bd6e4c90ec49b0a57006fda91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\frac{153}{3} = 51$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"111\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>We could have also realised that the median of consecutive integers is equal to the mean, so the middle would have to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027650310ea482223afc90bec0e5e1aa580361fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{153}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The largest number is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/f/dffbe7357cecc82fa2439f6ce462933cfe570b3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51 + 1 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } 52}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"141\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Verifying_Solution\">Verifying Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Verifying Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the largest integer of the three is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1d1611143f5792dc0f61f3b130af88cb790c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, then the other two integers must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1fd7cb028e27b8648efbfb002f3e6d4fcb33a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> because the three numbers are consecutive. The sum of these integers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e4dbd3509f7310fb81f47c6c10df325e41821bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50 + 51 + 52 = 101 + 52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"193\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f152e2688863b88e971932e82c28adec9063a05e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$153$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. This matches what the sum is supposed to be, so we have verified our solution.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_